Read `docs/operations/deployment-runbook.md` and
`docs/architecture/11-deployment-architecture.md` before changing deployment,
runtime configuration, or operational scripts.

Never expose, copy into source control, or modify secret values.

## Standard through-production path

EO may run the standard release when all of the following hold:

- exact accepted candidate
- committed SHA bound to that digest
- standard path `NEGOTAITIONS_YANDEX_POC`
- resolved Product target `.eo/deployment-targets/negotaitions-production.json`
- valid StandingReleaseGrant
- typed PREPARE / PREFLIGHT / DEPLOY / CANARY

On that path, do not demand repeated low-level approvals for internal
ssh/git/systemctl. Native Agent does not drive production by raw SSH.

## Exceptional operations

Still require explicit authority:

- destructive DB/data mutation
- force push / history rewrite
- arbitrary production shell
- unknown production script
- firewall/VPN/infrastructure mutation
- secret mutation outside the declared contract
- rollback with data-loss risk
- deploy of an unaccepted SHA

Raw Native production SSH mutation remains prohibited.
